; Tutorial_9_Conclusion.inix -- conclusion

[about]
Title=9 - Conclusion
Intro=What the walks covered, a glossary in two voices, and every way to get help with urlFido.
Setup=Nothing to set up; this walk only listens.
Homework=Fetch the documents from one page you visit often, and keep its folder.

[step]

Say=That is urlFido. Here is what each walk gave you.
Key=

[step]

Say=Walk one, the dialog. Walk two, installing. Walk three, a page's documents. Walk four, choosing what to fetch. Walk five, testing first.
Key=

[step]

Say=Walk six, several pages at once. Walk seven, pages behind a sign in. Walk eight, the command line.
Key=

[step]

Say=Now a short glossary. I say the term; the other voice says what it means.
Key=

[step]

Say=Extension.
Key=
Hear=The ending of a file's name, such as pdf or docx, that says what kind of file it is.

[step]

Say=Pattern.
Key=
Hear=A name with wildcards, a star for any characters and a question mark for one, matching several files at once.

[step]

Say=Source list.
Key=
Hear=A text file of page addresses, one to a line, fetched from in one run.

[step]

Say=Test fetch.
Key=
Hear=A run that works out what it would download, and downloads nothing.

[step]

Say=Main profile.
Key=
Hear=Your everyday Edge settings and sign ins, used instead of urlFido's own.

[step]

Say=Help is a key away: F1 in the dialog shows Help, and Shift plus F1 says the tip for the control you are on.
Key=F1
Hear=urlFido Help dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The full guide, in the help folder, has worked examples, the editing keys, and what to do when a page yields nothing. F11 checks for a newer version.
Key=

[step]

Say=The urlFido page on GitHub has the latest release and a place to report a problem; each run's log says exactly what happened.
Key=

[step]

Say=Thank you for listening. Happy fetching.
Key=
